-- ============================================================================
-- DR2 EXPERT DEEP SEED: Torque, Drag & Casing Wear, advanced tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, so the seeded structure and the
-- shipped lesson files cannot disagree.
--
-- What this tier owns: what the friction force does to the steel on both sides
-- of the contact. A string in compression is a column rather than a rope, with
-- two buckling limits whose ratio is exactly 2*sqrt(2) - 1 at every
-- inclination, in every hole and for every pipe, because both come from the
-- same expression; the limits are ZERO in a vertical hole and RISE with
-- inclination, and a tighter hole gives a HIGHER limit, which is why washouts
-- are a buckling concern. Two capacities checked independently with no
-- interaction term: tension utilization scales with the string's true vertical
-- depth and torsion with its contact length, so the two INVERT between a
-- vertical well and a lateral. Casing wear is the same side force spent over
-- rotating hours, its sliding distance depends only on the PRODUCT of rpm and
-- hours, and the volume-to-depth conversion is a crescent, so doubling the
-- wear factor raises the depth by about 1.6 rather than 2. And where the model
-- stops: lock-up is a positive feedback it structurally cannot predict, and
-- the disagreement with the independent oracle is stated in full with both a
-- relative and an absolute measure and the case that settles it.
--
-- Every number in the lessons is derived by running the vendored
-- engines/drilling against its own goldens, and the teaching lab that the
-- panels and this course share is pinned to the same values by
-- torquedragLab.test.js. A numeric sweep over the lessons resolved all 403
-- literals carrying seven or more significant figures to an engine-derived
-- value; a tier-leakage sweep over the lessons and the banks reports zero
-- downward leaks and zero same-tier answer prints against all eighteen graded
-- fields.
--
-- Answer keys live only here and in academy_quiz_questions, which has no
-- client SELECT policy.
-- ============================================================================

values ('torquedrag', 'advanced', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-compression","title":"Compression","lesson_keys":["l01-a-string-in-compression","l02-the-neutral-point-is-not-a-place","l03-the-sinusoidal-limit","l04-the-helical-limit","l05-the-ratio-that-does-not-move"]},{"key":"m02-what-the-pipe-has-left","title":"What the Pipe Has Left","lesson_keys":["l01-tensile-capacity","l02-torsional-capacity","l03-which-one-binds","l04-combined-loading"]},{"key":"m03-casing-wear","title":"Casing Wear","lesson_keys":["l01-the-same-side-force-over-hours","l02-sliding-distance","l03-the-crescent-groove","l04-the-wear-factor","l05-what-is-left-of-the-wall"]},{"key":"m04-planning-against-it","title":"Planning Against It","lesson_keys":["l01-where-the-wear-lands","l02-what-actually-reduces-it","l03-the-derated-burst","l04-the-uncertainty-it-inherits"]},{"key":"m05-when-the-model-stops","title":"When the Model Stops","lesson_keys":["l01-the-string-that-will-not-go-in","l02-lock-up","l03-extended-reach-and-what-limits-it","l04-a-disagreement-worth-knowing-about","l05-what-this-course-will-not-certify"]},{"key":"m06-the-expert-reading","title":"The Expert Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
